  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      186.55,
      451.24,
      214.82
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause amends section 3 of the Trusts Ordinance (Chapter 87) (hereinafterreferred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d), by the inclusion of the definitions of theexpressions \u201cbeneficiary\u201d and \u201cprescribed\u201d in that section.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      224.95,
      451.18,
      243.62
    ],
    "text": "Clause 3 : This clause inserts new sections 6A and 6B in the principal enactment and thelegal effect of\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      179.71,
      253.75,
      451.19,
      282.02
    ],
    "text": "(a)the new section 6A is to make provisions for the Registrar General tomaintain a register of trusts and to require the trustees to provideinformation relating to trusts to the Registrar General; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      179.71,
      292.15,
      451.15,
      310.82
    ],
    "text": "(b)the new section 6B is to make provisions for enabling the RegistrarGeneral to provide information of trusts to relevant authorities.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      320.95,
      451.18,
      339.62
    ],
    "text": "Clause 4 : This clause inserts new sections 19A, 19B and 19C in the principal enactmentand the legal effect of\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      179.71,
      349.75,
      451.18,
      368.42
    ],
    "text": "(a)the new section 19A is to require the trustees to keep updated informationin record on the identity of the persons connected with trusts;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      179.71,
      378.55,
      451.16,
      397.22
    ],
    "text": "(b)the new section 19B is to require the trustees to provide information torelevant authorities; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      180.43,
      407.35,
      451.19,
      426.02
    ],
    "text": "(c)the new section 19C is to impose penalties for offences committed undersections 6A, 19, 19A and 19B of the principal enactment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      436.15,
      451.18,
      454.82
    ],
    "text": "Clause 5 : This clause amends section 72 of the principal enactment, and is consequentialto the amendment made by inserting section 19C in the principal enactment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      464.95,
      451.18,
      483.62
    ],
    "text": "Clause 6 : This clause amends section 75 of the principal enactment, and is consequentialto the amendment made by inserting section 19C in the principal enactment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      139.15,
      493.75,
      451.21,
      522.02
    ],
    "text": "Clause 7 : This clause inserts new section 115A in the principal enactment, and the legaleffect of the section is to provide for the Minister to make regulations under the principalenactment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
